	(footprint "TS06:TS06_INS1_Lamp"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "64647870-9a28-590e-b43b-6216078c761b")
		(at 50.535 11.5)
		(descr "ИНС-1 colon neon, wire-ended. 5.0 mm nominal lead pitch, deliberately oversized pads/drill (2.2/1.0 mm) to absorb the +/-0.2 mm pitch measurement uncertainty against the FreeCAD reference model - same wire-landing philosophy as the fascia's panel hardware and the SEC IN-17 pads. Pad 1 is the lead nearer the board's TOP edge in this part's local frame. Silk outline: the measured 6.97 mm envelope as two arcs that stop short of the pads (the full circle ran through both). Pad 1 (square) is the ANODE, the lead the lamp marks with a dot - the opposite of the LEDs, whose square pad is the cathode - so the silkscreen carries a dot and an A beside it (30.09.26). Silkscreen lines 0.15 mm, the fab minimum.")
		(tags "neon INS1 colon THT wire-landing TERMINAL-06")
